equality.\n\n### 6. OUT-bound honesty — **PASS**\nMissing ledger and incomplete self-reported due set are documented and pinned.\n\n---\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Sev | Finding |\n|----|-----|---------|\n| **F1** | **MUST-FIX** | Full-width colon on Feedback label silently disables the hard rule (false green). |\n| F2 | Medium | Codex plugin manifest not bumped to 0.27.0; no version-equality guard. |\n| F3 | Low | G25m “would go green under json.loads” claim wrong for chosen key order. |\n| F4 | Low | 4 of 14 kinds lack paired G25 teeth. |\n| F5 | Note | Ledger `eval_id` presence/format not enforced (schema example only). |\n\nNot defects: absent-ledger silence, self-reported due incompleteness, no cross-layer join with `evals.json`.\n\n---\n\n## Decisions / deviations\n\nReviewed the `5c7068f` tree via blob import, not current HEAD. No edits.\n\n---\n\n## Open questions\n\nnone blocking. Optional: should non-empty unsatisfied ledger + missing Feedback also fail-closed? Currently silent by design; F1 is worse because Feedback *was* written.\n\n---\n\n## Verdict\n\n**REWORK**\n\nBlocking: **F1**. Ride-along: **F2–F4**.\n\n---\n\n## Next recommendation\n\n1. Fix Feedback parsing so full-width `：` is not “absent”; add a G25 tooth for unsatisfied due + `Feedback：positive`.\n2. Bump `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` (or add discover-all version equality).\n3. Optionally cover the four untested kinds; fix G25m narrative order.\n4. Re-run adversarial review on the fix before calling the hard rule production-safe.\n\n---\n\nFull write-up: `.hopper/handoffs/exp-p1-A-output.md`",
